<title>ZAIRE: Kabila says &quot;assumes&quot; Mobutu preparing to quit.</title>
<headline>Kabila says &quot;assumes&quot; Mobutu preparing to quit.</headline>
<dateline>LUBUMBASHI, Zaire 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zairean rebel leader Laurent Kabila said on Sunday he assumed that Zairean President Mobutu Sese Seko was preparing to give up power, meeting the rebel condition for calling off an assault on the capital.</p>
<p>Kabila told Reuters in Lubumbashi by telephone from the South African navy ship Outeniqua, where he is about to meet Mobutu: &quot;I am still waiting for Mobutu to board the ship and I can only assume that his delay in arriving is because he is preparing his exit from power.&quot;</p>
</text>
